  "articleBody": "Hiring a contractor to upgrade your garage sounds simple until you realize how many trades might be involved. Garages are often treated like basic storage boxes, but bringing them up to speed with fresh framing, drywall, durable flooring, updated wiring, and better insulation requires serious planning. Before you sign any contract, it pays to know exactly what you are getting into.\n\nFirst, clarify your goals. Are you building out a clean workshop, adding custom cabinetry, or upgrading walls and lighting? Your intended use dictates whether you need mechanical, electrical, or structural permits alongside general building permits. Second, have the existing structure checked out. A cracked slab, sagging rafters, or outdated electrical service can quickly derail a cosmetic remodel if they are not spotted beforehand. Third, verify contractor scopes. You want a written agreement specifying who pulls permits, who manages inspections, and how specialized trade work like electrical or plumbing is handled.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\nYour garage’s current condition makes all the difference. Older garages may hide foundation shifts or framing defects that require structural work before any finish carpentry or drywall begins.\n\nWhen you are ready to update your space, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your garage remodeling goals.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
